                <pb facs="0997" n="983" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg983"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Registration/66: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-22T20:00:00-04:00">March 22, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>370. A number of American firms which have done business in China in the past are
                    discussing with officers of the Department the question of registration under
                    Chinese laws and regulations. They are making a study of the Chinese regulations
                    governing the registration of firms promulgated in 1931 and propose to request
                    the Department to present their views on this matter to the appropriate Chinese
                    authorities through the Embassy. In the meantime, they have requested to be
                    informed whether the Chinese authorities have set any “deadline” for the
                    registration of American and other foreign companies which have offices or
                    representatives in Free China at the present time. The Department would
                    appreciate receiving by radio any information you may have on this point.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
